          "filename": "Black Hills Central Railroad Company - 63 diesel locomotive (GP9) (Hill City, South Dakota, USA) (37586387664).jpg",
          "caption": "(photo by Lee St. John)\n\n\nThis diesel locomotive belongs to a tourist railroad in the Black Hills of western South Dakota.  The engine is a General Motors Electro-Motive Division GP9 that was built in November 1956 and became Chesapeake &amp; Ohio Railway # 6178.  It has also seen service as Indiana &amp; Ohio Railway # 63, Chillicothe-Brunswick Rail Maintenance # 63, and Progressive Rail # 63.",
