          "filename": "Black Hills Central Railroad Company - 104 steam locomotive (Baldwin 2-6-2T) (Hill City, South Dakota, USA) (38247801786).jpg",
          "caption": "(photo by Lee St. John)\n\n\nThis 2-6-2T steam locomotive belongs to a tourist railroad in the Black Hills of western South Dakota.  The engine was built in 1926 by Baldwin Locomotive Works and became Peninsula Terminal Company # 104 in the Pacific Northwest.  The \"T\" in the model designation refers to a tank locomotive.  Such engines carried a water tank(s), instead of using a tender car for storing water.",
